1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:42,410
It's almost like a maze in here.

22
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:44,370
Try not to get lost.

23
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:45,450
Okay.

24
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:50,460
Oww...

25
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:51,080
Are you okay?

26
00:01:51,290 --> 00:01:52,630
Sorry.

27
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:57,920
What's this?

28
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:00,260
D-Dynamite!

29
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,260
Seriously?!

30
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:05,680
They're all damp now.

31
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,480
Don't worry; they won't explode.

32
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,850
Come on; get a move on.

33
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,650
We don't know when the enemy will come after us.

34
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:16,440
Right.

35
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:24,280
Looks like the blizzard died down.

36
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:27,250
Get ready.

37
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:28,120
Aye, sir.

38
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:35,630
We're going to take down Kimblee and his
two men from Central when we see an opening.

39
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:38,880
Aye, sir.

40
00:02:41,910 --> 00:02:44,910
The Abyss

41
00:02:41,910 --> 00:02:44,910
The Abyss

42
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:56,730
We're going to proceed with the mission with only the men currently present.

43
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,610
Don't tell anyone; not even soldiers from Northern Headquarters.

44
00:02:59,610 --> 00:03:00,150
Hey-

45
00:03:00,150 --> 00:03:01,820
Major Miles!

46
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:03,910
By "bring down", do you mean you're going to kill them?!

47
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:05,910
Of course.

48
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:08,370
I don't approve killing.

49
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:11,580
It's better to seal their abilities and beat information out of them.

50
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:14,080
Do you really think he'll tell the truth?

51
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,040
It's dangerous to keep him alive.

52
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,800
Then what about his men?

53
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:22,720
They may also be obeying him without choice after being turned into chimeras!

54
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:27,220
You have a point, but the keyword here is "may".

55
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:30,390
So you're going to kill them simply based on suspicion?

56
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:33,850
Same with Lieutenant General Raven! There were plenty of other methods-

57
00:03:33,850 --> 00:03:35,900
Do not forget the law of Briggs.

58
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,860
If you let your guard down, you die.

59
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:44,110
Your softness may come back to kill you or one of your friends someday.

60
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:50,450
We don't need careless men in this land.

61
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:53,750
We're going to get rid of Kimblee and his two men.

62
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:01,710
I guess he's still a kid, after all.

63
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:02,970
Yeah.

64
00:04:02,970 --> 00:04:06,640
Trying to settle matters without deaths in this world is a soft idea in itself.

65
00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:09,760
But there was a time I was like that, as well.

66
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:12,270
I was, too.

67
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:16,520
You start to understand once you reach this age after living through many battles...

68
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:20,780
...that it's more difficult to keep someone alive rather than killing them.

69
00:04:21,610 --> 00:04:25,240
The Elric Brothers chose the tougher path.

70
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,240
Strange guys, aren't they?

71
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:28,870
Yeah.

72
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:31,540
But I'm also a bit envious.

73
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:42,000
What's this "Rasayana" he writes about?

74
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,260
It's used to describe a miraculous medicine that extends one's lifespan.

75
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:48,180
I wonder if he's talking about a philosopher's stone?

76
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,390
Let's see...

77
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:57,270
What is this "Aurelian" that "turns all metal to gold,
and transforms old men to adolescents"?

78
00:04:57,850 --> 00:04:59,020
It's a word for gold.

79
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:02,690
Most of this talks about immortality and gold.

80
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:08,410
Could it be because Mr. Scar's brother was heavily influenced by Eastern Alchemy from Xing?

81
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,070
Meaning?

82
00:05:10,070 --> 00:05:15,000
In my country, we refer to the immortal as a "True Being".

83
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:20,170
It literally means "Perfect Being",
but because gold is a perfect metal,

84
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:23,250
there are times we refer to
a "True Being" as a "Golden Being".

85
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:30,510
I see. So a perfect being is a golden being.

86
00:05:30,850 --> 00:05:34,890
Some say we refer to them that way because
the person who introduced alchemy to Xing...

87
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:40,770
...was an immortal man with golden hair and eyes.

88
00:05:40,770 --> 00:05:42,150
Wow...

89
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:46,990
Golden hair and eyes? Sounds like Ed and Al!

90
00:05:47,990 --> 00:05:49,450
Hey guys, come here!

91
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:50,240
I found the exit!

92
00:05:58,790 --> 00:06:00,290
The sun's so bright!

93
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,960
Looks like we were able to get through the mountain.

94
00:06:03,290 --> 00:06:04,750
The weather looks nice.

95
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:07,380
Let's head to Briggs now while we can.

96
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,800
Okay, everyone. Follow me-

97
00:06:11,090 --> 00:06:12,970
Looks like the snow is pretty deep.

98
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:12,470
Help me!

99
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:13,930
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

100
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:14,970
You can ride on my back, little girl.

101
00:06:13,930 --> 00:06:15,390
Help me!

102
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:19,850
We'll make a path through the snow, so you can follow us.

103
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,350
You guys listening?!

104
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:18,810
Hey! Hey! Hey!

105
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:21,310
Help me!

106
00:06:19,850 --> 00:06:21,310
We appreciate it.

107
00:06:30,530 --> 00:06:32,660
Hey!

108
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,790
Hey! Help me!!!

109
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,290
Is someone there?!

110
00:06:38,290 --> 00:06:39,210
Al?!

111
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:41,290
Sir Alphonse?!

112
00:06:41,830 --> 00:06:42,830
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

113
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:44,290
Are you okay, Al?!

114
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:47,710
You saved me...

115
00:06:48,090 --> 00:06:51,220
I got stuck in a deep spot and ended up getting buried by the snow.

116
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,890
But why are you here, Al?

117
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:56,600
I crossed the mountain to get here before you guys.

118
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:59,770
You crossed the mountain... in that blizzard?

119
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:05,940
I get it. Instead of making a detour here, you took a straight path.

120
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,440
But why make such a reckless trip?

121
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:10,320
I have urgent news.

122
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,820
"Urgent news"?

123
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:15,950
The Central Army has infiltrated Briggs.

124
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:21,660
Apparently, Major General Armstrong has been summoned to Central, as well.

125
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:25,040
So it's dangerous to go there now.

126
00:07:27,090 --> 00:07:28,300
What should we do?

127
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,590
We can't go back, either.

128
00:07:31,130 --> 00:07:34,090
You're going to have to find somewhere else to hide out.

129
00:07:34,090 --> 00:07:36,140
Yeah, like where?

130
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,020
Follow me.

131
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:44,980
Where are we going?

132
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:49,480
There should be a village by the name of Asbec not too far from here.

133
00:07:50,150 --> 00:07:54,360
I've heard rumors my fellow countrymen have taken refuge in the slums there.

134
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,700
An Ishbalan slum, huh?

135
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:59,080
Doesn't seem like we have much of a choice.

136
00:07:59,450 --> 00:08:01,500
Master, you rock! Let's get going!

137
00:08:06,330 --> 00:08:08,210
But is it going to be okay?

138
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:09,250
What is?

139
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:13,050
Won't Sir Kimblee get suspicious if you disappear all of a sudden?

140
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:16,970
Nothing to worry about. Brother will keep everything under control.

141
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:20,060
Three from the third squadron.

142
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,060
Five from the fourth squadron.

143
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,100
Looks like we're all here.

144
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:27,650
Now, I want you all to begin searching in the districts you've been assigned.

145
00:08:27,650 --> 00:08:28,110
Yes, sir.

146
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:29,020
Roger.

147
00:08:33,610 --> 00:08:34,450
Let's move.

148
00:08:34,450 --> 00:08:35,740
Aye, sir.

149
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,820
Come on, Alphonse.

150
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:40,870
Isn't this where you say "Okay"?

151
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:46,370
But it's really hard to move in this, Edward.

152
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:48,420
That's where I need you to do your best.

153
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,130
Come on, Kimblee's watching.

154
00:08:51,250 --> 00:08:53,010
Wait up, Brother!

155
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:54,300
Walk faster.

156
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:06,020
Hey. Where are Kimblee and company searching?

157
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,810
There's a huge mine shaft at the center of the town, right?

158
00:09:08,810 --> 00:09:11,820
Apparently, they're going to enter that and search the mine.

159
00:09:14,110 --> 00:09:19,070
He said he's only going to take the men he brought from Central because he doesn't trust the soldiers up here.

160
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,990
He must have noticed already.

161
00:09:23,490 --> 00:09:24,450
We're going to stall them.

162
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:27,460
Secure a position for sniping near the shaft mine.

163
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:27,960
Roger.

164
00:09:38,130 --> 00:09:40,640
Search the entrance to the mine.

165
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:43,350
If you find multiple footprints, there's no doubt.

166
00:09:43,350 --> 00:09:43,890
Yes, sir.

167
00:09:48,810 --> 00:09:49,770
Can you do it?

168
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:51,810
At this distance, yes.

169
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:57,280
What's wrong?

170
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,320
Edward is...

171
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,030
What?

172
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:11,500
Kimblee, shouldn't you leave it to the soldiers from Briggs to search the mines?

173
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:14,000
I heard it's a labyrinth down there.

174
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:19,970
Seeing as how you went through the effort to persuade me out of it, this must be the place.

175
00:10:19,970 --> 00:10:21,430
What are you talking about?

176
00:10:22,010 --> 00:10:23,890
I just want to capture Scar-

177
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:27,600
Or are you trying to buy time to position the sniper?

178
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:30,600
So you noticed?

179
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:34,650
There's so much thirst for blood in the atmosphere; it would be odd not  to notice.

180
00:10:35,070 --> 00:10:37,900
I didn't survive Ishbal for nothing.

181
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:41,740
It looks like they're talking about something. What should I do, sir?

182
00:10:42,530 --> 00:10:44,330
Can you try to adjust your aim on Kimblee?

183
00:10:44,330 --> 00:10:45,160
Yes.

184
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,450
Do it. Be very careful.

185
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:48,290
Aye, sir.

186
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:02,510
That bastard hid himself in snow!

187
00:11:02,510 --> 00:11:03,890
Dammit!

188
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,220
Kimblee!

189
00:11:09,140 --> 00:11:10,390
Damn you...

190
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:30,000
So you two are chimeras, too, huh?

191
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:07,200
Shit... I can't see a thing.

192
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:09,660
Well, they can't see me either...

193
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,990
...so I guess we're even-

194
00:12:12,450 --> 00:12:15,710
Quit resisting, Fullmetal Alchemist!

195
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:21,130
There's no way for you to run since we can track you by scent!

196
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:22,970
Shut up!

197
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:32,730
Fullmetal!

198
00:12:34,730 --> 00:12:35,890
What's going on?!

199
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,360
Where are you?! Respond!

200
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,110
Is that you, Major Miles?!

201
00:12:40,110 --> 00:12:41,690
There are chimeras here!

202
00:12:41,690 --> 00:12:44,570
And they've been trained to fight in places with low visibility!

203
00:12:44,570 --> 00:12:47,320
Stay out of the smoke!

204
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,460
Oww...

205
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:02,380
Dammit... that just made me shorter...

206
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:05,800
Dynamite?

207
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,050
We're in a mine, all right!

208
00:13:12,890 --> 00:13:15,430
Don't get too close now!

209
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:17,270
You do know what these are, right?

210
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:18,560
Are you stupid?

211
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:21,610
Those are probably too damp to use.

212
00:13:21,610 --> 00:13:25,150
Do you two know what dynamite is made of?

213
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,860
Nitroglycerine?

214
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:31,370
Nitroglycol, chips of wood, and...

215
00:13:31,370 --> 00:13:33,450
...ammonium nitrate, maybe?

216
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:37,750
Then what's ammonium nitrate made of?

217
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:40,380
Easy! Nitric acid and ammonia-

218
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:45,210
Ammonia?!

219
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:50,510
The smell!!!

220
00:13:56,930 --> 00:13:58,390
What's that smell?!

221
00:13:58,390 --> 00:13:59,940
Ammonia.

222
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:02,860
I guess there's a downside to having too keen a sense of smell.

223
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:05,400
These guys are toast.

224
00:14:06,190 --> 00:14:10,700
So this is how you're going to act as soon as your hostages are released?

225
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:12,990
Don't know what you're talking about.

226
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:17,410
I'm just here to beat all the information you know out of you.

227
00:14:18,290 --> 00:14:20,670
Christ, you're so hot-blooded.

228
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:25,050
Fighting with a young man like yourself during
my convalescence would surely break my bones.

229
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,630
And I don't have time to play with you either.

230
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,800
I guess I'll be using this, then.

231
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,720
He just saved me the trouble of searching for it!

232
00:14:40,270 --> 00:14:41,140
He's fast!

233
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:50,820
Too slow!

234
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:59,080
He lost his philosopher's stone,
and his transmutation circle is no longer useable!

235
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:00,250
I-

236
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:01,330
"I win!"

237
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,290
Is that what you're thinking?

238
00:15:04,250 --> 00:15:06,210
The determination not to kill.

239
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:08,630
An admirable policy.

240
00:15:08,630 --> 00:15:12,800
But that's just asking for your enemy to take advantage of you during battle.

241
00:15:13,390 --> 00:15:17,850
You should have killed me at that moment.

242
00:15:21,310 --> 00:15:24,610
That softness is the cause of your defeat.

243
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:05,020
Did I fall down the mine shaft?

244
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:11,860
He's so heartless... he even got us into it...

245
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:13,450
Oww...

246
00:16:13,450 --> 00:16:14,820
Dammit...

247
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:16,950
Where did Kimblee go...

248
00:16:23,210 --> 00:16:24,670
You've got to be kidding me...

249
00:16:24,670 --> 00:16:25,710
Hey!

250
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,270
Al! What's wrong?!

251
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:53,070
Sir Alphonse?!

252
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:53,860
Al?!

253
00:16:55,570 --> 00:16:56,570
This isn't good.

254
00:16:57,030 --> 00:16:58,780
I'm being drawn again...

255
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:02,370
What do you mean, "being drawn"?

256
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:03,580
Hey, what's wrong?

257
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:03,580
Al?

258
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,710
My soul...

259
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:08,630
...is being drawn toward...

260
00:17:11,670 --> 00:17:12,630
Al!

261
00:17:12,630 --> 00:17:13,460
Al?!

262
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,590
His soul is being drawn?

263
00:17:14,050 --> 00:17:15,590
Sir Alphonse?!

264
00:17:15,590 --> 00:17:19,260
Has this happened before?

265
00:17:15,590 --> 00:17:18,760
Sir Alphonse! Pull yourself together!

266
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:20,300
I don't know!

267
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,010
PLACEHOLDER

268
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,890
Sir Alphonse!

269
00:17:21,010 --> 00:17:21,890
Al?

270
00:17:21,890 --> 00:17:24,470
Wake up, Al!

271
00:17:24,890 --> 00:17:25,810
No...

272
00:17:25,810 --> 00:17:26,520
Al!

273
00:17:26,850 --> 00:17:27,980
Al!!!

274
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:30,060
What...

275
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,110
What should I do?!

276
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,610
Ed!

277
00:17:44,450 --> 00:17:49,790
I can't... let her cry over something stupid like this...

278
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:09,350
Damn that Kimblee...

279
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,820
Yo, Fullmetal.

280
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:16,940
You alive?

281
00:18:17,650 --> 00:18:19,700
Why did you save us?

282
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:21,870
You're hurt far worse than us.

283
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:25,620
Don't... get the wrong idea...

284
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:30,580
I... need someone to pull...

285
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:33,880
...this thing out... of my abdomen.

286
00:18:34,250 --> 00:18:37,050
You're asking us to pull that steel frame out of you?

287
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:38,720
We're technically enemies, you know.

288
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:40,840
Yeah... please.

289
00:18:44,850 --> 00:18:48,770
Well, we weren't ordered to kill you or anything.

290
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:50,890
Let's see.

291
00:18:50,890 --> 00:18:55,690
But if we pull that out,
you're going to bleed out in an instant.

292
00:18:56,150 --> 00:19:02,780
As soon as it leaves my body... I'm going to seal the wound... before I bleed to death.

293
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:07,200
Are you experienced in medical alchemy at all?

294
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:14,420
I've attempted human transmutation in the past... so I studied the main points.

295
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:18,880
"The main points"? I'm pretty sure your organs are shredded to pieces...

296
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:22,050
If you don't have a philosopher's stone like Sir Kimblee does...

297
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:27,510
That's why I'm going to use my life instead of a philosopher's stone...

298
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:28,520
What?!

299
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:33,270
It may shorten my life span by a bit, though...

300
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:34,230
Is that okay?

301
00:19:34,730 --> 00:19:37,150
I don't have the time to dawdle.

302
00:19:37,150 --> 00:19:43,530
If this injury was caused by my softness... then I have to clean up after myself.

303
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:49,370
I don't really get it, but you don't have much time to waste.

304
00:19:50,330 --> 00:19:51,290
I'm pulling it out.

305
00:19:58,420 --> 00:19:59,590
Do it, please.

306
00:20:00,670 --> 00:20:04,800
I need to think of my life as a form of energy...

307
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:12,930
The same as... a philosopher's stone!

308
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:18,060
That's right!

309
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:22,070
Right now, I'm nothing more than
a philosopher's stone made out of one soul!

310
00:20:26,530 --> 00:20:31,120
Think back, and try to remember that feeling!

311
00:20:32,450 --> 00:20:33,790
That feeling...

312
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:35,750
...of using...

313
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:39,460
...life!!!

314
00:20:58,020 --> 00:20:59,190
Is he dead?

315
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:04,030
Don't just write me off like that...

316
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:06,280
Oh, it worked?!

317
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:09,160
It's not completely healed.

318
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:17,370
It's just a temporary measure of linking the undamaged tissues... to stop the bleeding.

319
00:21:17,670 --> 00:21:20,000
Then we need to get you to a doctor!

320
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,920
No, I don't have time... for that...

321
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,550
H-Hey!

322
00:21:25,550 --> 00:21:27,720
I need to go after Kimblee...

323
00:21:28,050 --> 00:21:31,430
...else... everyone will be in danger...

324
00:21:34,390 --> 00:21:35,680
Geez...

325
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:36,980
Idiot.

326
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:39,770
There's no way he can win against him in this state.

327
00:21:43,780 --> 00:21:44,900
What is it?

328
00:21:45,990 --> 00:21:47,280
Whoa...

329
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:49,280
A philosopher's stone, huh?

330
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,320
The one Sir Kimblee had with him, right?

331
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:53,330
You don't need to refer to that freak as "Sir".

332
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:56,620
He dragged us into this.

333
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:58,250
You're right.

334
00:21:58,250 --> 00:22:00,830
I guess that's the last time we see that bastard.

335
00:22:00,830 --> 00:22:02,000
Yeah.

336
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:05,380
People will think we died here, so we're free.

337
00:22:06,210 --> 00:22:08,840
And what should we do about him?

338
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:12,720
We can't just let him die.

339
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:15,020
He saved our lives.

340
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:17,560
Well said.

341
00:22:18,350 --> 00:22:21,230
We need to find a doctor right away
once we get out of here.

342
00:22:21,230 --> 00:22:22,270
Yeah.

343
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:46,210
The promise we never made

344
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:46,210
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

345
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
yet again

346
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
Kyou mo

347
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:51,840
tries to snatch our future away from us.

348
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:51,840
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

349
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:57,430
Why is it that we can't rejoice

350
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:57,430
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

351
00:22:57,430 --> 00:22:58,430
straight from the heart

352
00:22:57,430 --> 00:22:58,430
Sunao ni

353
00:22:58,430 --> 00:23:03,400
when we obtain something we've always been after?

354
00:22:58,430 --> 00:23:03,400
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

355
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:09,110
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

356
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:09,110
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

357
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,910
They're fragments born from agony.

358
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,910
Itami ga unda kakera de

359
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,950
Of all the moments and destinies,

360
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,950
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

361
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:27,710
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

362
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:27,710
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

363
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,260
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

364
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,260
Genkai datte konnan datte

365
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:34,260
I refuse to give up.

366
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:34,260
Akirametakunaiyo

367
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:39,140
Please, don't let go.

368
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:39,140
Konomama hanasanaide

369
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:46,980
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

370
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:46,980
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

371
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:50,650
where it's tightly joined with my left.

372
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:50,650
Koko ni arukara

373
00:23:58,870 --> 00:24:05,170
After breaking the stalemate,
unforeseen ideas and actions open new paths.

374
00:24:06,130 --> 00:24:10,380
The one to find the hidden truth obtains the key to victory.

375
00:24:10,710 --> 00:24:14,880
But that's all a part of the accumulating daily life.

376
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:20,180
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

377
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:24,200
Signs of a 
Counteroffensive

378
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:24,200
Episode 42, Signs of a Counteroffensive.

379
00:24:24,190 --> 00:24:26,860
The beginning of war.
